{title: 041 - O Splendor of God's Glory Bright}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G/D]O [Em]splendor [C]of [Am]God's glory [G]bright,
[Em]From [C]light [D7/C]eternal [G/B]bringing light;
[Am]O [D7]Light [G]of [C]life, [Bm/F#]light's [Em]living [Am]spring,
[Am/C]True day, [Bm]all days [Am]illumining.

Verse 2:
[G/D]O [Em]Thou true [C]Sun, [Am]on us [Bm]Thy [G]glance
[Em]Let [C]fall [D7/F#]in [G]royal radiance;
[Am]The [Bm]Spirit's [Am]sanctifying beam
[Am/C]Upon [Bm]our earthly [G]senses stream.

Verse 3:
[G/D]O [Em]joyful [C]be [Am]the passing [G]day
[Em]With [C]thoughts [D7/C]as clear [G]as morning's ray,
[Am]With [D7]faith [G]like [C]noontide [Em]shining [Am]bright,
[Am/C]Our souls [Bm]unshadowed [G]by the night.

Verse 4:
[G/D]Dawn's [Em]glory [C]gilds [Am]the earth [Bm]and [G]skies;
[Em]Let [C]Him, [D7/C]our perfect [G/B]morn, arise;
[Am]The [D7]Father's [C]help [Bm/F#]His [Em]children [Am]claim,
[Am/C]And sing [Bm]the Father's [Am]glorious [G]name. Amen.
